Summary

Writing a literature review is a rewarding task with added perks, such as


painting a picture on what the scientific literature in your topic really looks like;


pulling out studies that are relevant to your topic and showing your organizational skills in making sense of them;


displaying your creativity in designing the literature review that best supports and complements your study;


exercising critical thinking by looking at the studies from various perspectives; and


writing a logical, critical, and analytical literature review that supports your proposed study and naturally ends with your research question(s) or hypotheses.





